The Origin of Jesus Christ (Luke 3:23-38)
This is the genealogy of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham:
Abraham begot Isaac. And Isaac begot Jacob. And Jacob begot Judah and his brothers.
And Judah begot Perez and Zerah by Tamar. And Perez begot Hezron. And Hezron begot Aram.
Aram fathered Aminadab. And Aminadab fathered Nahshon. And Nahshon fathered Salmon.
And Salmon begot Boaz from Rahab. And Boaz begot Obed from Ruth. And Obed begot Jesse.
And Jesse brought King David. After this, David brought Solomon from the woman whom Uriah had taken.
And Solomon fathered Rehoboam. Rehoboam fathered Abijah. And Abijah fathered Asa.
Asa begot Jehoshaphat. And Jehoshaphat begot Joram. And Joram begot Uzziah.
Azariah fathered Jotham. Jotham fathered Ahaz. Ahaz fathered Hezekiah.
And Hezekiah fathered Manasseh. And Manasseh fathered Amon. And Amon fathered Josiah.
And Josiah brought Jeconiah and his brothers when the Jews were exiled in Babylon.
And after their exile period in Babylon ended, Jeconiah fathered Shealtiel. And Shealtiel fathered Zerubbabel.
And Zerubbabel begot Abiud. And Abiud begot Eliakim. And Eliakim begot Azor.
And Azor begot Zadok. And Zadok begot Achim. And Achim begot Eliud.
Eliud begot Eleazar. Eleazar begot Matthan. Matthan begot Jacob.
And Jacob brought Joseph, the husband of Mary who gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Messiah.
And so we find fourteen generations from Abraham to David, and fourteen generations from David to the exile to Babylon, and fourteen generations from the exile to Babylon until the coming of the Messiah. The birth of Jesus Christ (Luke 2:1-7)
And this is how Jesus Christ was born: When Mary, his mother, was engaged to a man named Joseph, and before they married, she conceived by the power of the Holy Spirit.
Brother, Youssef decided to break off his engagement with her to stay away from her without exposing her, because he was a man who feared God.
And he was still pondering the matter, when an angel from the Lord appeared to him in a dream and said to him: "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to marry Mary. She is pregnant by the power of the Holy Spirit,
And to bring a child, you shall name him Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins.
And all this happened to fulfill the words that God said through the mouth of the Prophet who said:
# Isaiah 7:14 The young woman will conceive and give birth to a child, who will be called "Immanuel." (Meaning "God is with us")
And when Joseph woke up, he did as the angel from God had told him, and took his wife to his home.
But he did not sleep with her until she gave birth to the child, and he named him Jesus.
The Wisdom of the Sages
When Jesus was born in Bethlehem, in the region of Judea, during the time of King Herod, a group of wise men from the East came to Jerusalem.
And they said: "Where is the king of the Jews who is born? We saw his star appear in the East, so we have come to worship him."
And when King Herod heard this, he was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him.
And the chief priests and the scribes of the Jews gathered together and asked them about the place where the Christ was to be born.
Answer them: "In Bethlehem, in the region of Judea, because this is what the prophet wrote in the book:
Micah 5:2 And you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, though you are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come for me one who will be ruler over Israel, whose origins are from of old, from ancient times.
Herod cried out to the wise men without listening to anyone and asked them about the time when the star appeared,
And he sent them off to Bethlehem and said to them: "Go and find the child. When you find him, come and tell me so that I too may go and worship him."
After they heard the king's words, they left. And while they were on the road, the star they had seen earlier in the east appeared before them, walking ahead until it reached and stopped above the place where the child was.
And when they saw the star, they were very happy,
They entered the house and found the child with his mother Mary. They immediately got off their mounts and prostrated to him, then opened their bags and presented him with gold, incense, and myrrh.
And their Lord warned them in the dream not to return to Herod, so they took another route and went back to their country. The escape to Egypt
And after the wise men left, the angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream and said to him: "Get up! Take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt and stay there until I tell you when to return, because Herod is going to search for the child and kill him."
Man, Youssef got up, picked up the child, and his mother died at night, and he went to Egypt.
# Hosea 11:1; Exodus 4:22 And he lived there until Herod died, to fulfill what the Lord had spoken by the prophet: "Out of Egypt I called my son." The massacre of the innocents in Bethlehem
And when Herod saw that the wise men had mocked him, he became very angry and ordered the killing of all the children in Bethlehem and the surrounding areas who were two years old and under, according to the time the wise men had told him.
Oh man, what the prophet Jeremiah said has come true:
# Jeremiah 31:15 "In Ramah, they heard a loud cry and bitter weeping and wailing, Rachel weeping for her children and refusing to be comforted, because they are no more." The return from Egypt to Nazareth
And when Herod died, the angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream, while he was in Egypt,
They said: "Get up! Take the child and his mother and return to the land of Israel, because those who wanted to kill him are dead."
The man stood up, picked up the child and his mother, and returned to the land of Israel.
But when Archelaus became king of Judea in place of Herod, he was afraid to go there. So God warned him in a dream, and he went to the region of Galilee.
And he went to a city called Nazareth and lived there so that what the prophets said would be fulfilled: "He will be called a Nazarene."
The Announcement of John the Baptist (Mark 1:1-8; Luke 3:1-18; John 1:19-28)
