I baptize you with water for repentance, but the one who is coming after me is mightier than I, and I am not worthy to carry his sandals. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and fire.
He shakes the bundle of the board in his hand and clears the harvest in the hall, gathers the wheat in the storehouse, but the straw is burned with an unquenchable fire." John baptizes Jesus (Mark 1:9-11; Luke 3:21-22)
And Jesus came from the region of Galilee to the Jordan to be baptized by John.
But John would not let him and said, "I need to be baptized by you, how is it that you come to me?"
But Jesus answered him, "Let this thing happen now, because this is how we fulfill all the righteous things." So John agreed.
And when Jesus was baptized, he came up out of the water, and immediately the heavens were opened; behold, he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove and resting on him.
And a voice from heaven said: "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased."
Jesus is tempted by Satan (Mark 1:12-13; Luke 4:1-13)
And the Holy Spirit led Jesus into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil.
The guy fasted for forty days and forty nights until he got hungry.
