The Sermon on the Mount (Luke 6:20-23)
And Jesus, the light of the people, went up the mountain and sat down, and at that time his disciples came to him,
And he began to teach them and said:
Bless their souls, the poor! They are the kingdom of the heavens to be taken.
Good health to them, the sad ones! They are going to be honored.
Good health to the good people! They are the land to be inherited.
Health to those hungry and thirsty for the truth! They are about to be satisfied.
Bless those who show mercy! They will be shown mercy.
Blessed are those whose hearts are pure! They are the face of God to be seen.
Bless those who reconcile between people! They are God's children to be named.
Health to those who suffer for the sake of truth! The kingdom of the heavens will be theirs.
Good health to you when people insult you, torment you, and say all the bad things about you—it's all on my mind!
Rejoice and jump for joy, for your reward is great in heaven. This is how the prophets before you were also persecuted." Salt and light (Mark 9:50; Luke 14:34-35)
You are the salt of the earth, but if the salt loses its flavor, how can it be restored? It is no longer good for anything; it will be thrown out and people will trample on it.
You are the light of the world. There is no city built on a hill that cannot be seen,
There is no one who lights a lantern and puts it under a bowl, but rather puts it in a high place and it lights up the whole house.
Let your light shine before others, so they may see your good works and glorify your Father in heaven.» The Law
Don't think that I came to abolish the law and the prophets; I did not come to abolish them but to fulfill them.
I tell you the truth: Until the heavens and the earth pass away, not a letter or a single dot of the law will disappear until everything is accomplished.
Whoever disobeys one of the least of these commandments and teaches others to do the same will be called least in the kingdom of heaven. But whoever obeys them and teaches others to do so will be called great in the kingdom of heaven.
I tell you, unless you become more righteous than the teachers of the Jews and the Pharisees, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven." Cheating
Exodus 20:13; Deuteronomy 5:17; 16:18 "You have heard what was said to your ancestors: 'You shall not kill, and whoever kills must be judged.'"
But now I tell you: whoever gets angry at his brother must be judged by the court, and whoever calls his brother "ignorant" must be judged by the Jewish council, and whoever calls his brother "beast" must go to hell.
What if, while you are offering your gift at the altar, you remember that you have a problem with your brother,
Leave your offering in front of the altar, and first go and be reconciled with your brother; then come and present your offering.
And if someone complains about you, reconcile quickly while you are on your way to the court, so that he does not complain about you to the judge, and the judge talks to the police about you and you end up in jail.
I'll tell you the truth: you won't get out of there until you pay the last penny." Adultery
# Exodus 20:14; Deuteronomy 5:18 "You have heard what was said to your ancestors: 'You shall not commit adultery.'"
But I am telling you that whoever desires a woman and covets her, he has committed adultery with her in his heart.
If your eye causes you to sin, pluck it out and throw it away; losing a part of your body is better for you than having your whole body thrown into hell.
And if your hand causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away; it is better for you to lose one part of your body than for your whole body to go into hell. Divorce (Matthew 19:9; Mark 10:11-12; Luke 16:18)
# Deuteronomy 24:1-4 "And it is also said: 'He who divorces his wife must give her a certificate of divorce.'"
But I am telling you: He who divorces his wife for a reason other than adultery causes her to commit adultery, and he who marries a divorced woman is committing adultery.» Al-Halfan
# Numbers 19:12; Numbers 30:2; Deuteronomy 23:21 "And you heard the command given to your ancestors: 'Do not swear falsely, but be truthful in what the Lord has promised.'"
