But I tell you: do not take revenge when they do evil to you. But if someone strikes you on your right cheek, turn the other one also.
Whoever wants to fight you to take you away, let him also take your cloak.
If someone forces you to go with him for one kilometer, go with him two.
"To the one who asks you for something, give it to him, and to the one who wants to borrow from you, do not refuse him." Love your enemies (Luke 6:27-28, 32-36)
Have you heard what is said: "Love your neighbor and hate your enemy."
But I tell you: love your enemies and pray for those who persecute you,
So that you may be children of your Father in heaven. For He causes His sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the righteous and the unrighteous.
What reward do you deserve if you want those who love you? Isn't it those who collect taxes who do this with their own hands?
And what did others decide if you only handed it over to your sisters? Isn't it true that those who don't know God do this by themselves?
