Charity
Be careful to do good deeds in front of people so they can see you; otherwise, you will have no reward from your Father in heaven.
When you give charity to someone, don't blow a horn like hypocrites do in mosques and streets so that people thank them. I'll tell you the truth: they have already received their reward.
But you, when you give charity, let not your left hand know what your right hand is doing,
"Let your charity be in secret, and your Father who sees in secret will reward you." Prayer (Luke 11:2-4)
And when you pray, do not be like the hypocrites, for they love to stand and pray in the synagogues so that people may see them. Truly, I tell you, they have received their reward.
But you, when you pray, go into your inner room, close the door, and pray to your Father who is unseen. And your Father who sees in secret will reward you.
And when you pray, do not keep repeating meaningless words like other peoples who think that God will listen to them because they say many words.
Don't be like them, because your father knows what you need before you ask for it.
So pray like this: Our Father in heaven, hallowed be your name.
Let your kingdom come to us, let your will be done, on earth as it is in heaven.
Give us each day our daily bread.
Forgive us our sins, just as we forgive those who wrong us.
We did not enter into an experiment, and we were saved from evil.
And if people forgive each other's mistakes, then He who is in the heavens will also forgive your sins.
But if people do not forgive others for their mistakes, even your Father in heaven will not forgive your sins.» Fasting
And when you fast, do not show sadness on your faces like the hypocrites, who disfigure their faces to show people that they are fasting. I tell you the truth: they have received their reward.
But you, when you fast, comb your hair and wash your face,
"Let your fasting not be seen by others, but by your Father who is unseen; and your Father who sees what is done in secret will reward you." Wealth (Luke 12:33-34)
Do not store up for yourselves treasures on earth, where moth and rust destroy, and where thieves break in and steal.
But store up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust destroys, and where thieves do not break in or steal.
"Where your treasure is, there your heart will be also." Light of the body (Luke 11:34-36)
The eye is the lighthouse of the body. So if your eye is healthy, your whole body will be filled with light.
But if your eye is diseased, your whole body will be full of darkness. If the light within you is darkness, how great is that darkness! God or money (Luke 12:22-31; 16:13)
No one can serve two masters; they will either hate one and love the other, or be devoted to one and despise the other. You cannot serve both God and money.
Why don’t I tell you not to worry about your life, what you will eat or what you will drink, or about your body, what you will wear. Isn’t life better than food, and the body better than clothing?
Look at the birds of the sky: they do not sow or reap or store in barns, yet your Father in heaven feeds them. Aren't you much better than they are?
And which one of you who thinks can add an hour to his life?
And why worry about the outfit? Look at the Boukraoun flower how it grows: it neither tires nor spins.
But I tell you: even King Solomon in all Megiddo did not wear a single one like them!
If God wears weed like this outfit, then weed grows today and tomorrow it will be thrown into the oven fire, so how much more should you be dressed, you whose faith is weak!
That's why you shouldn't worry and ask: What are we going to eat? Or what are we going to drink? Or what are we going to wear?
All these things are sought after by people who are not believers, and your Father in heaven knows that you need them.
But you seek first the kingdom of God and His righteousness, and these things will also be given to you.
That's why you shouldn't worry about tomorrow; tomorrow will take care of itself. Each day has enough trouble of its own.
Do not judge others (Luke 6:37-38, 41-42)
"Don't judge people so that you won't be judged."
The judgment you pass on others is the one that will be passed on you, and the measure you use for others will be used for you.
Why do you see the speck in your brother's eye, but don't notice the plank in your own eye?
And how can you tell your brother: "Let me take the speck out of your eye" when you have a plank in your own eye?
O hypocrite! Remove the plank from your own eye first, and then you will be able to see clearly and remove the speck from your brother's eye.
