Ask and you shall receive, seek and you shall find, knock and it will be opened to you.
Indeed, whoever asks receives, whoever seeks finds, and whoever knocks will have the door opened.
Who among you, when asking your child for bread, gives him a stone?
And when they ask for a fish, he gives them a snake?
If you, the wicked, know how to give good things to your children, then how much more will your Father in heaven give good things to those who ask Him?
Rather, do to others the things you want them to do to you. This is what the law and the prophets have said.» The Narrow Door (Luke 13:24)
Enter through the narrow gate. Because the gate to destruction is wide and easy, and many enter through it.
